==Croatian==

===Etymology===
There are several theories about its origin. It may be connected with Greek {{term|ἀδάμας||tr=adamas||diamond}}, or come from {{etyl|fro}} {{term|alemande}}<ref>[[:w:Petar Skok|Petar Skok]], Etimologijski rječnik hrvatskoga ili srpskoga jezika, Z., 1971, v. 1, p. 28, ''alem'': ''mislim da se u alem može da sakriva grčka riječ adāmas »dijamant« ... Ali treba pomišljati i na to da se može raditi o istoj riječi alemande, koja dolazi u spomenutom starofrancuskom Pelerinage-M''</ref>. Another possibility is {{etyl|ota|sr}} {{rfv-etymology}} {{term|عالم|tr=âlem|sc=ota-Arab|lang=ota}} ({{etyl|tr|hr}} {{term|alem|lang=tr}}) < {{etyl|ar|sr}} {{term|عالم|tr=ʕālam|sc=Arab|lang=ar}}.

===Noun===
{{hr-noun|m}}

# [[jewel]], [[gem]]
# [[world]]

====Synonyms====
* (''jewel''): {{l|hr|alem-kamen}}

